## What changed

The [original incident page](/kb/incidents/4471) says "one issue, one fix queued".
Its rendered cause table contradicts that claim: one merged ticket contains two
separate failure paths. A fix to the shared parser will not correct the booking form's
hint. The table also shows that the hint reports have no ticket of their own.

<Callout>
This is an investigation of the export dated 2026-10-04, not a live queue.
The desk keeps working: refresh the export and rebuild before making a current
operational claim. "Known" and "queued" do not mean fixed.
</Callout>

## Separate engineering tickets

- [Shared parser reads day-first dates month-first](https://github.com/przemos/megadev-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1).
  The shared parser reads month first although these tenants write day first.
  App and email reports take this path; form reports do too when their form hint
  is day-first. Use the tenant directory, not the reporter's browser language.
- [booking-v3 gives day-first tenants a month-first hint](https://github.com/przemos/megadev-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2).
  The form prints `MM/DD/YYYY`, people follow it, and the form reads their input
  in the tenant's day-first order. This path is limited to form reports from
  day-first tenants on booking-v3: Alder Physio, Copper Studio and Pale Harbour.

Counts, affected tenant counts, intake tags and observed date ranges below run
from the exported reports and tenant files at render time. The two groups are
disjoint and together account for every unique report merged into the ticket.

