## Change the triage rule, not just this ticket

The [accepted subject-line decision](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) and
[triage prose](/kb/triage/dedupe) disagree with the executable dedupe explorer.
The triage page was reviewed in June 2024; its rendered stale warning matters.
An identical subject can hide different causes, while different subjects can
describe the same failure path. Neither the subject nor the intake tag proves
that two reports are duplicates.

The [replacement decision](/kb/decisions/0002-dedupe-by-cause) is proposed for
desk approval. It preserves the accepted record rather than rewriting history.
Use tenant locale, form version, channel and report evidence to identify a cause.
Keep unknown tenants and conflicting evidence for manual review.

## Verification and impact

The kb identifies sched-prod as serving about 300k people. That is product context,
not an affected-user count; this export counts reports, not distinct people.
Do not infer a timezone defect from a one-day description alone, or claim a
parser fix will resolve the separate hint issue.

Rebuild both the original and correction pages, check the computed totals, and
run the regression tests. Confirm each issue's fix independently with ambiguous
day/month inputs and all affected channels before closing it. Continue to watch
new received reports rather than treating merge throughput as recovery.

